          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            All
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
            may be realized as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
            applied not necessarily to the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
            itself, but to the result of regarding each of its strands as resolved by some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of strands.
          %p
            We state this precisely as Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AllHorizontalWeightSystemsAreslNWeightSystems"}
            below (due to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BarNatan96"} Bar-Natan 96
          %h2#Ingredients Ingredients
          %p
            Given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            (or in fact just any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
          %p
            1) write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}^{pb}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+vector+space"} modulo
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2T+relations"} 2T relations
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4T+relations"} 4T relations
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HorizontalChordDiagramsModulo2TAnd4T.jpg", :width => "900"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
          %p and write
          #eq:SpaceOfHorizontalWeightSystems.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒲
                    %mi pb
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{W}_{pb}
                  \\coloneqq
                  (\mathcal{A}^{pb})^\ast
          %p
            for its degreewise
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
            = succeed ";" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+weight+systems"} horizontal weight systems
          %p 2) write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi n
                    %mi pb
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}
                  \\overset{
                  \\;\;\; p_n \;\;\;
                  }{\longrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}_n
                  \\overset{
                  \\;\;\; i_n \;\;\;
                  }{\hookrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}
          %p
            for projection onto and inclusion of the linear subspace spanned by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            strands;
          %p 3) write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\mathbb{N}}{\oplus} \mathbb{N}
                  \\overset{
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\Delta^{(-)}
                  \\;\;\;
                  }{\longrightarrow}
                  End( \mathcal{A}^{pb} \big)
          %p
            for the operation that reads in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \coloneqq (k_1, \cdots, k_n)
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi k
                      %mo |
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi sum
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\vert k\right\vert \coloneqq \underset{i}{sum} k_i
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
          #eq:Delta.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi n
                    %mi pb
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi k
                      %mo |
                    %mi pb
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo |
                          %mi k
                          %mo |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi pb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}
                  \\overset{
                  \\;
                  p_n
                  \\;
                  }{\to}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}_{n}
                  \\overset{
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\Delta^k
                  \\;\;\;
                  }{\longrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}_{\left\vert k \right \vert}
                  \\overset{
                  \\;
                  i_{\left\vert k \right\vert}
                  \\;
                  }{\hookrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{A}^{pb}
          %p
            which takes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            strands to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
            of chord diagrams obtained by replacing its
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_i
            strands for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and then summing over all ways of re-attaching chords, with any vertex previously on some strand
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            now to be put on one of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_i
            strands (
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan96"}> Bar-Natan 96, Def. 2.2
            ).
          %p For example:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HorizontalChordDiagramPartitioning.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HorizontalChordDiagramPartitioningGenericII.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
